---
/**
 * /privacy — first-pass Privacy Policy.
 *
 * A working draft in the site's plain-language register for counsel to
 * review, replacing the "being prepared" placeholder. It describes what
 * the site and product actually do today: analytics off by default
 * behind the consent banner, the Google Fonts caveat, the beta-request
 * form, Cedar chat, and the product's customer content. Positions kept
 * deliberately favorable: aggregated and de-identified improvement use,
 * standard service-provider and legal disclosures, and rights handled
 * through one contact address.
 */
import { site } from '../config';
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | Lumecon"
  description="Privacy Policy for the Lumecon platform and its entry-point domains: Local Economic Impact, Tribal Economic Impact and Global Economic Impact. Covers data collection, use, retention and Cedar AI handling."
  canonical="https://lumecon.ai/privacy"
  keywords="Lumecon privacy policy, data privacy, economic impact analysis privacy, Cedar AI privacy, tribal economic data privacy"
>
  <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
  <div class="date">Working draft, under review by counsel.</div>

  <h2 class="legal-subhead">What we collect</h2>
  <p>
    We collect what you give us and what operating a website requires, and little else. When you
    request beta access or contact us, that is your name, work email, organization, role and
    whatever you tell us about what you want to measure. When you use the product, it holds the
    documents and figures you bring to your analyses. When you talk to Cedar on this site, the
    conversation is processed to answer you and reviewed in aggregate to improve the answers; do
    not put sensitive information in a chat. Our servers keep the short-lived technical logs any
    web service keeps.
  </p>

  <h2 class="legal-subhead">How we use it</h2>
  <p>
    We use contact and beta-request details to respond, to grant access and to tell you about the
    service you asked about. We use product content to run your analyses and support you. We use
    aggregated and de-identified information to improve the model and the platform; improvement
    work does not identify you or your organization. We do not sell personal information, and we
    do not use your information for third-party advertising.
  </p>

  <h2 class="legal-subhead">Analytics and your consent</h2>
  <p>
    Analytics are off by default. We use privacy-friendly product analytics only after you opt in
    through the consent banner, to understand which parts of the site are useful and to improve
    them. One note on fonts: our pages load the Inter and JetBrains Mono typefaces from Google
    Fonts, which means your browser requests those font files from Google's servers (sending the
    IP address any web request carries). This is font delivery, not analytics; no consent state
    changes it. If you decline, or until you choose, no analytics or tracking scripts run, no
    analytics cookies are set, and no usage beacon is sent. You can change your mind at any time
    through the Privacy choices control in the footer of every page, which presents the consent
    banner again.
  </p>

  <h2 class="legal-subhead">When we share</h2>
  <p>
    We share information with service providers who host and operate the platform for us, under
    obligations to protect it; when the law requires it; to protect the service, our customers or
    the public from harm; and as part of a financing, acquisition or similar transaction, in which
    case this policy continues to apply to the information transferred. That list is complete.
  </p>

  <h2 class="legal-subhead">Retention and security</h2>
  <p>
    We keep information for as long as it serves the purpose you gave it to us for, plus what the
    law and good records practice require, and then delete or de-identify it. Product content is
    retained while your organization's account is active. We protect information with measures
    appropriate to its sensitivity, and no method of transmission or storage is perfectly secure.
  </p>

  <h2 class="legal-subhead">Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    Write to <a class="note-link" href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> to ask what we
    hold about you, to correct it or to have it deleted, and we will respond within the time the
    applicable law sets. The service is for organizations and is not directed to children.
  </p>

  <h2 class="legal-subhead">Changes</h2>
  <p>
    We will update this policy as the service evolves. Material changes will be posted here with a
    new date, and where the law requires it we will tell you directly.
  </p>

  <div class="note">
    <strong>Counsel:</strong>{' '}{site.counsel}<br />Contact: <a
      href={`mailto:${site.email}`}
      class="note-link">{site.email}</a
    >
  </div>
</LegalLayout>
